FFmpeg (libavcodec, libavutil)
------------------------------
Optional. The MPEG-1 still-image and FMV decoders link the shared
`libavcodec` and `libavutil`. This project does not modify FFmpeg and does not
carry FFmpeg source in this tree.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Source builds link whichever FFmpeg is installed,
and the applicable license is that build's: distribution builds that enable
`--enable-gpl` are GPL-2.0-or-later.

Release packages bundle FFmpeg 9.0.2 built by `packaging/ffmpeg/build-ffmpeg.sh`
from the unmodified upstream source tarball
(https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz, SHA-256
`8c3850283eb25fa026482078a04051e0be17347b09ef81a0849bec15a96e002e`). The build
is shared and LGPL only: neither `--enable-gpl`, `--enable-version3` nor
`--enable-nonfree` is set, nothing is auto-detected, and only the MPEG-1 video
and MPEG audio layer II decoders and parsers are compiled in. The libraries
are shipped as separate files (`libavcodec`, `libavutil`, `libswresample`
where present), so they can be replaced with a build of your own made from the
same source. `FFMPEG_SOURCE.txt` in each package names the source tarball.

Full LGPL-2.1 text: `third_party/licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt`
Source: https://ffmpeg.org/


